1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,583
Zoya's wall is covered in notes.

2
00:00:02,583 --> 00:00:03,896
The farmer, Mrs.

3
00:00:03,896 --> 00:00:07,647
Rao, the new bakery, jaggery
prices, a new food rule.

4
00:00:07,947 --> 00:00:10,017
Too much to think about at once.

5
00:00:10,017 --> 00:00:11,375
She needs two boxes.

6
00:00:11,725 --> 00:00:15,968
Marketers call them the microenvironment
and the macroenvironment.

7
00:00:16,568 --> 00:00:19,363
The family sorts the notes
on the kitchen table.

8
00:00:19,663 --> 00:00:21,751
Close and personal in one box.

9
00:00:21,751 --> 00:00:23,899
Big and far away in the other.

10
00:00:24,499 --> 00:00:26,077
So what is the difference?

11
00:00:26,377 --> 00:00:30,897
Kotler and Armstrong say the
microenvironment is the actors close to the

12
00:00:30,897 --> 00:00:34,559
company that affect its
ability to serve its customers.

13
00:00:34,859 --> 00:00:39,767
The macroenvironment is the larger
forces in society that affect the whole

14
00:00:39,767 --> 00:00:41,041
microenvironment.

15
00:00:41,341 --> 00:00:43,332
Micro means small and near.

16
00:00:43,332 --> 00:00:45,218
Macro means big and wide.

17
00:00:45,818 --> 00:00:47,963
Start with the microenvironment.

18
00:00:47,963 --> 00:00:49,913
Follow one pack of laddoos.

19
00:00:50,213 --> 00:00:51,113
Suppliers.

20
00:00:51,055 --> 00:00:54,215
A farmer sells Nani the
ragi and the jaggery.

21
00:00:54,515 --> 00:00:55,543
The company.

22
00:00:55,543 --> 00:00:59,612
Nani cooks, Arjun sells, Dev
designs, and Zoya decides.

23
00:00:59,912 --> 00:01:03,957
Intermediaries help a company
sell, deliver and get paid.

24
00:01:03,957 --> 00:01:04,857
Mrs.

25
00:01:04,509 --> 00:01:07,180
Rao pays by UPI, through her bank.

26
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:08,380
Customers.

27
00:01:08,265 --> 00:01:09,165
Mrs.

28
00:01:08,760 --> 00:01:10,950
Rao and the other tiffin parents.

29
00:01:11,250 --> 00:01:12,161
Competitors.

30
00:01:12,161 --> 00:01:15,196
The new bakery, chasing
the same tiffin box.

31
00:01:15,496 --> 00:01:18,812
And publics, groups who
watch and talk about you.

32
00:01:18,812 --> 00:01:20,598
Like the families in Mrs.

33
00:01:20,598 --> 00:01:21,660
Rao's building.

34
00:01:22,260 --> 00:01:24,136
Micro is who you deal with.

35
00:01:24,136 --> 00:01:26,556
Macro is the world they all live in.

36
00:01:27,256 --> 00:01:29,046
Now the macroenvironment.

37
00:01:29,046 --> 00:01:31,123
Kotler names six big forces.

38
00:01:31,423 --> 00:01:33,769
Demographic, who people are.

39
00:01:33,769 --> 00:01:38,921
In 2023, the United Nations estimated
India had become the world's most

40
00:01:38,921 --> 00:01:40,359
populous country.

41
00:01:40,659 --> 00:01:43,279
Economic, how much people can spend.

42
00:01:43,279 --> 00:01:46,430
When prices rise, families
watch every rupee.

43
00:01:46,730 --> 00:01:48,939
Natural, weather and resources.

44
00:01:48,939 --> 00:01:51,953
A poor sugarcane season
makes jaggery costly.

45
00:01:52,253 --> 00:01:54,029
Technological, new tools.

46
00:01:54,029 --> 00:01:56,753
Parents can now pay by phone in seconds.

47
00:01:57,053 --> 00:01:58,943
Political, laws and rules.

48
00:01:58,943 --> 00:02:02,194
A new label rule changes
what the pack must say.

49
00:02:02,494 --> 00:02:04,469
Cultural, beliefs and habits.

50
00:02:04,469 --> 00:02:07,296
More parents want
healthy, home style food.

51
00:02:07,596 --> 00:02:11,007
Many teams use a similar
checklist called PESTLE.

52
00:02:11,007 --> 00:02:15,802
Political, economic, social,
technological, legal and environmental.

53
00:02:16,402 --> 00:02:18,369
Where do we see this at work today?

54
00:02:18,669 --> 00:02:19,569
Suppliers.

55
00:02:19,539 --> 00:02:23,730
A hospital keeps two medicine
suppliers, in case one fails.

56
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:24,993
Competitors.

57
00:02:24,993 --> 00:02:27,873
A phone maker studies every rival launch.

58
00:02:28,173 --> 00:02:29,446
Economic forces.

59
00:02:29,446 --> 00:02:33,407
An airline offers cheaper
seats when families spend less.

60
00:02:33,707 --> 00:02:34,607
Technology.

61
00:02:34,589 --> 00:02:37,492
A bank moves its services onto your phone.

62
00:02:38,092 --> 00:02:40,177
But are these maps always useful?

63
00:02:40,177 --> 00:02:41,939
Only if you use them well.

64
00:02:42,239 --> 00:02:43,250
The good side.

65
00:02:43,250 --> 00:02:46,192
A checklist makes sure you
don't miss anything big.

66
00:02:46,492 --> 00:02:47,570
The hard side.

67
00:02:47,570 --> 00:02:51,902
Forces overlap, lists get old fast,
and a map doesn't tell you what to

68
00:02:51,902 --> 00:02:52,802
do.

69
00:02:52,641 --> 00:02:55,398
Dev makes a giant chart with forty notes.

70
00:02:55,698 --> 00:02:58,653
Zoya circles just three
that matter this month.

71
00:02:58,653 --> 00:03:02,240
Jaggery prices, the bakery,
and the healthy food trend.

72
00:03:02,540 --> 00:03:03,928
A map shows the world.

73
00:03:03,928 --> 00:03:05,921
You still have to choose the path.

74
00:03:06,221 --> 00:03:07,121
The lesson?

75
00:03:07,100 --> 00:03:10,089
Map everything, then act
on what matters most.

76
00:03:10,689 --> 00:03:11,654
Quick check.

77
00:03:11,654 --> 00:03:14,321
A new bakery opens next to the college.

78
00:03:14,321 --> 00:03:17,595
Is that part of the micro
or the macroenvironment?

79
00:03:19,495 --> 00:03:20,395
Micro!

80
00:03:20,124 --> 00:03:25,050
A competitor is an actor close to
Laddoo Lab, chasing the same customers.

81
00:03:25,650 --> 00:03:26,659
So, remember.

82
00:03:26,959 --> 00:03:31,764
The microenvironment is the actors
close to you: suppliers, intermediaries,

83
00:03:31,764 --> 00:03:34,156
customers, competitors and publics.

84
00:03:34,506 --> 00:03:38,079
The macroenvironment is the
big forces that shape them all.

85
00:03:38,429 --> 00:03:42,332
Check them with a list like PESTLE,
then act on what matters most.

86
00:03:42,932 --> 00:03:46,318
Next time, we'll explore
marketing information systems.
